-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----
PLACEHOLDER — Replace this file with your real VMC certificate.

A Verified Mark Certificate (VMC) is an X.509 certificate issued by an
accredited Certificate Authority that ties your BIMI logo to your domain.

How to obtain a VMC:
  1. Your domain must have a published DMARC policy of p=quarantine or p=reject.
  2. Purchase a VMC from an accredited CA:
       • DigiCert  — https://www.digicert.com/tls-ssl/verified-mark-certificates
       • Entrust   — https://www.entrust.com/digital-security/certificate-solutions/products/digital-certificates/verified-mark-certificates
  3. The CA will verify your trademark registration before issuing the cert.
  4. Replace this entire file with the PEM-encoded certificate chain they provide.
     The real file starts with:  -----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----
     and ends with:              -----END CERTIFICATE-----

Without a valid VMC, BIMI logos still display in some clients (Apple Mail,
Fastmail) but NOT in Gmail. Gmail requires an Authority Evidence Document (AED)
pointing to a VMC.

Once you have the real .pem, upload it here and update your BIMI DNS record:
  default._bimi.yourdomain.com  TXT  "v=BIMI1; l=https://yourdomain.com/logo.svg; a=https://yourdomain.com/vmc.pem"
-----END CERTIFICATE-----
